//? Title: Guided backpropagation:unchanged logits and a modified backward rule
//? Requires: vanilla_saliency.mepml
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Gradient-based image visualizations can change when the backward propagation rule changes. Freeze the verified MNIST classifier and compare ordinary derivatives with a positive-positive guided rule,including every sign/zero gate and real-image target/weight controls.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/guided_backprop.cpp`.

> The method

At a ReLU with pre-activation a and incoming signal g,the guided rule returns g*1[a>0]*1[g>0]. Forward ReLU values remain identical. Because the extra gate depends on the incoming signal,the rule is nonlinear in g and is not the derivative VJP of that forward function.

$$ G(a,g)=g\,1[a>0]1[g>0]. $$
\alttext(Guided backpropagation retains the incoming signal only when both the forward activation and incoming signal are strictly positive.)

No classifier fitting occurs here. Restore the exact selected and actual-initial arrays produced by the explicit tensor-Adam loop in vanilla_saliency;all model computations and control statistics remain tensors.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/guided_backprop_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/guided_backprop_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/guided_backprop_concept.tikz > build/guided_backprop_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/guided_backprop_concept.svg build/guided_backprop_concept.dvi > build/guided_backprop_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
